<p>President Trump warned Iran on Sunday to move quickly toward a peace deal with the United States, saying on Truth Social that time was running out and warning of severe consequences if Tehran did not act. The warning followed stalled talks aimed at ending a war that began when U.S. and Israeli forces launched major strikes on Iran on Feb. 28, with Washington pressing demands that include limits on or dismantlement of Iran&#x27;s nuclear program and missile stocks. Washington and Tehran agreed to a truce on April 8, but negotiations have not produced a settlement. Iranian state-linked media said the United States had not offered concrete concessions in response to Tehran&#x27;s latest proposals. The warning came before Trump&#x27;s planned discussions with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu about the Middle East crisis. The conflict has shaken energy markets and drawn Israel and Lebanon into a parallel conflict involving Hezbollah. Saudi Arabia said it intercepted three drones that entered its airspace from Iraq, and Oman condemned the Barakah drone strike.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oZE1vLCOWZceZgYvLIvDpLyWaFdZeRLXKCS4-ZaKQCgWWCpr-zegAt_LfOzx4ZgL5mvp31hzu0QGoZiwn5P2YjJE4c7SdljkBF7_eSqUuYzgig4xlsXkqqaR3wh8gLfvh64nSoqgckYxnH8yUyRxu6u9KHuCaad8pd4xm2HCItdgY0eiqivecP3_zpo0eaAkPigsknadkHzdD_vGIIMfBHy6OwJl3RlQNkrz_mG9-HM36h6uvUEKeO6IFw-NyAt00ucMSw_OzJP3-xKCJ9jGy41ytr4w0Jk' alt='Donald Trump has issued a new warning against Iran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Military options: Axios, cited by Al Arabiya and Bankier, said President Trump was expected to convene a Situation Room meeting on Tuesday to discuss military options against Iran.</li><li>Hormuz dispute: President Trump said the United States, not Iran, controlled the Strait of Hormuz, while an Iranian official said Tehran would soon present a plan to allow some traffic through the strait for a fee.</li></ul><blockquote>For Iran, the Clock is Ticking, and they better get moving, FAST, or t